title five verbs: a rename, a death, a fresh hard-linked pair, an edit

# The genuinely blind cross-check between the two emission
# compilers: the kernel lane wrote its prediction down before this
# side ran, and neither had seen the other's number.
#
# It exists because the first real agreement covered a link and a
# write, which are the two easiest verbs. Rename, materialize and
# the death of a whole object were all uncrossed -- and the death
# path is the one the kernel lane got wrong in its first draft, so
# it is where a disagreement was most likely.
#
# Onto is quiet throughout, so nothing conflicts and nothing is
# held: the fixture is entirely about what compiles, not about what
# quarantine suppresses.

tree base
  1-1: /
    5-100: a = av0
    6-100: b = bv0
    7-100: doomed = dv0

tree onto
  1-1: /
    5-100: a = av0
    6-100: b = bv0
    7-100: doomed = dv0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    5-100: a2 = av0
    6-100: b = bv1
    8-300: fresh = fv0
    8-300: fresh2
